Data cache false sharing
========================

Part of HW_Specific: tests that stress one hardware resource, to study how
interference on it shows up in other partitions. The sizes come from
BENCH_TOOLS/arch_config.h (cache and TLB geometry of the target).

What it tests
-------------

False sharing: two partitions write to different addresses that map to the same
data-cache sets. If the RTOS manages the caches correctly the WCET is not
affected.

What it does
------------

Two partitions, P1 and P2, one periodic process each.

In each partition a process walks a growing address range (from L1D/4 up to
half the last-level cache), aligned to a chosen cache set, writing every other
line 100 times per period, and reports the WCET, ACET and BCET of each walk
size.

Expected output
---------------

"Starting new walk: Start / End / Step / Dataset size" and "End walk: WCET ACET
BCET"; "Benchmark END" when all sizes are done.

Notes
-----

The name says TODO: the authors marked the test as unfinished.

Build and run
-------------

From the top-level directory (builds every benchmark; QEMU needs only the one):

    make benchmarks                     # x86_64
    make BSP=arm64-qemu benchmarks      # arm64

    qemu-system-x86_64 -vga none -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/HW_Specific/CACHES/DCACHE_PRIVATE_FSHARING_TODO/build/x86_64-qemu/pok.elf
    qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a53 -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/HW_Specific/CACHES/DCACHE_PRIVATE_FSHARING_TODO/build/arm64-qemu/pok.elf

To build only this benchmark, run "scons bsp=x86_64-qemu" (or bsp=arm64-qemu)
in this directory with POK_PATH set. The benchmark runs forever; quit QEMU with
Ctrl-A X.
